@startuml
!include style.iuml
' Sources: RobotExecution.cpp; ClientPrograms.cpp; ServerPrograms.cpp;
' ControllerAdmission.cpp. Lifelines represent objects, not one thread per object.
title Axis / robot finite move · reservation, planning and start
caption Source-level successful path plus rejection gates. This is not a hardware qualification claim.
footer ICC lifeline = both bridges + transports + queues; it is not an additional application class.
autonumber
actor "CLI caller" as CLI
box "M7 · UI" #EDF4FE
participant "Robot\nplanning worker" as R
participant "Client\njob registry" as C
end box
boundary "Serialized ICC\nnormal lane" as W #FFF5DF
box "M4 · IO" #EAF7F4
participant "Server\ndispatch + command worker" as S
participant "Controller\n+ Ownership" as O
participant "Executor" as E
participant "STEP HAL\nTIM2 / DMA" as H
end box

CLI -> R : submit(ExecutionRequest)\nAxis facade or Robot move
R -> C : create(family, selected axes)
C --> R : job ID
R -> R : enqueue planning request; notify
R --> CLI : job ID immediately
note over CLI,C #EDF4FE
  Returning to the prompt does not destroy the job.
  Robot.run() performs planning on its dedicated worker.
end note

== Acquire an authoritative starting state ==
R -> C : inspect() / model validation
C -> W : io/trajectory: Inspect
W -> S : request ready; notify IO dispatcher
S -> O : control(Inspect)
O --> S : boot ID, capabilities, positions, references
S --> W : Reply
W --> C : decoded reply
C --> R : model / hardware capabilities
R -> C : acquire(job, configuration fingerprint, axes)
C -> W : io/trajectory: Acquire
W -> S : dispatch deferred service
S -> O : control(Acquire)
O -> O : atomic family / axis admission
alt Busy, stale boot, unavailable hardware or invalid configuration
  O --> S : error + busy job when applicable
  S --> W : rejection
  W --> C : mark Rejected
  C --> R : stop planning this request
else Reservation obtained
  O --> S : token + commanded positions + axis revisions
  S --> W : authoritative reservation snapshot
  W --> C : store boot / token with job
  C --> R : snapshot
  note over C,O
    Client.run() renews active ownership every 50 ms.
    M4 expires an unrenewed lease after 250 ms.
  end note
  R -> R : convert units, validate path, quantize endpoint\ncompile one normalized progress profile
  note right of R #EDF4FE
    FiniteProgram contains profile description,
    signed displacements and axis limits.
    Cartesian point moves interpolate in joint space.
  end note

  == Prepare locally on M4; outputs are not started ==
  R -> C : execute(job, reservation, FiniteProgram)
  C -> W : io/trajectory: Prepare\nboot + token + configuration + positions + revisions
  W -> S : deferProgram(): queue bounded command
  S -> O : [command worker] prepareProgram()
  O -> O : verify lease, revisions, positions, references, limits
  O -> E : prepare(command, bind_outputs=false)
  note over O,E #EAF7F4
    Numerical preparation runs outside Controller's mutex.
    Reservation keeps the selected axes owned.
  end note
  E -> E : validate progress; build nominal + stopping schedules
  E --> O : prepared or error
  O -> O : reacquire mutex; revalidate epoch / reservation / axes
  alt Preparation fails, is cancelled, or becomes stale
    O --> S : explicit rejection; no start
    S --> W : deferred Reply
    W --> C : reject job; request reservation Release
  else Preparation remains valid
    O -> E : bind() via StepperMotor::prepareCoordinated()
    E -> H : bind per-axis schedules / DIR; stage initial buffers
    O --> S : Staged
    S --> W : finishProgramCommand(): deferred Reply
    W --> C : preparation succeeded

    == Run is a separate action ==
    C -> W : io/motion goal: Run{boot, token, job}
    W -> S : admitProgram(Run, execution)
    S -> O : startProgram(Run, completion callback)
    O -> O : final ownership / revision / hardware checks
    O -> E : start(token)
    E -> H : start prepared outputs on common timeline
    O --> S : success
    S --> W : action accept()
    W --> C : on_accepted → Running
    note over C,H #FFF5DF
      In the current code, startProgram() precedes action acceptance.
      A STEP edge may occur before the UI receives acceptance.
      Zero-displacement programs complete without arming outputs.
    end note
  end
end
@enduml
